<% title "Invite Your Parent or Guardian" %>
<% page_full %>

<%# Fuime: what the parent's signature gates depends on the money model, and
    this page has to say the true one (ONBOARDING_PLAN §4.1, L8). Under
    merchant-of-record the guardian requirement sits at the payout seam
    (Event#payout_setup_blockers) — a teen can keep setting up first. Under
    Connect it sits at activation (Event::Application#activation_blockers). The
    old copy promised "your venture will be fully activated", which under MoR
    described a gate that is not there.

    It deliberately does NOT say "you can start selling now": selling under MoR
    waits on Fuime's human vetting (Fuime::OperatorEligibility), not on the
    parent, and this page is usually reached before that decision. What is true
    here is only that the parent is not what holds up the teen's setup. %>
<% merchant_of_record = ::Fuime::Features.merchant_of_record? %>
<main class="center max-w-xl card mt4 md-p3 mx-auto">
  <h1 class="mt0 border-0 mb-2">Invite your parent or guardian</h1>

  <p class="text-lg mb-4">
    Since you're under 18, Fuime needs a parent or guardian to be the legal signer
    and responsible adult on your account. They'll be able to see your business activity.
    <% if merchant_of_record %>
      You can keep setting up. Your parent or guardian signs before you get paid.
    <% else %>
      Your venture can't go live until they sign.
    <% end %>
  </p>

  <%= render "application/callout", type: "info" do %>
    <strong>What happens next:</strong> We'll email them a link to read and accept the
    guardian agreement.
    <% if merchant_of_record %>
      Until they accept, you can't be paid.
    <% else %>
      Once they accept, your venture can be activated.
    <% end %>
  <% end %>

  <%= form_with model: @guardianship, url: guardianships_path, class: "mt-4" do |f| %>
    <div class="field mb-3">
      <%= f.label :guardian_email, "Parent or Guardian's Email", class: "block mb-1 font-bold" %>
      <%= f.email_field :guardian_email,
                        class: "input w-full",
                        placeholder: "parent@example.com",
                        required: true,
                        autofocus: true %>
    </div>

    <div class="flex justify-center mt-4">
      <%= f.submit "Send Invitation", class: "btn bg-accent" %>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <%# Fuime performs no identity verification today — Guardianship#accept! records a
      checkbox, a timestamp, an IP and a user agent, and the Guardian Agreement itself
      says so in §6. This copy previously promised the parent would "verify their
      identity", which the product does not do; saying so was the overclaim, not the
      missing feature. Reword here when real verification ships, not before. %>
  <p class="text-sm muted mt-4 text-center">
    Your parent will receive an email asking them to read and accept the
    <%= link_to "Guardian Agreement", guardian_agreement_path, class: "underline" %>,
    which makes them the legal signer for your venture. Accepting confirms they agree
    to that responsibility; it is not an identity check.
  </p>
</main>
